WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:08.240
The Waikiwi Memorial Gates are first mentioned&nbsp;
in the 1961 domain inspection report. There is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:13.920
additional archive between 1959 and 1961 of&nbsp;
money from Internal Affairs for the funding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.880
of a war memorial. The Invercargill City Council
took ownership for the Waikiwi Domain Board&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:24.400
in 1963.  These gates are likely built by the&nbsp;
Domain Board to recognize the Second World War&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.360
separately as the pavilion that was removed&nbsp;
in 1988 from Waikiwi Domain was a memorial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:35.040
pavilion dedicated to the First World War.&nbsp;
The park is inscribed "Waikiwi Memorial Park

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:42.400
dedicated to the memory of those who served and&nbsp;
made the supreme sacrifice World War Two 1939-1945"

